# E0.2 restart survival, run 2 of 2. Reads the persisted scale back.
#
# Runs against the SAME `TURNSTONE_ROOT` `browser_zoom_restart.scn` left
# behind, in a fresh process. No zoom row is committed here: every value below
# comes from the restored node and the session the shell respawned for it, so
# `page-zoom-applied` also witnesses that the restored request was replayed
# INTO the new engine rather than merely remembered beside it.
#
# Start scenarios/fixtures/browser_zoom_server.ps1 on port 43117 first (the
# restored node respawns its content, which refetches the fixture page).
settle 30
key escape
settle 120
assert focused 127.0.0.1:43117/zoom
assert content-live
assert snap page-zoom-requested == 125
assert snap page-zoom-applied == 125
assert snap ui-zoom == 110
capture 01_restart_run2_replayed
log E0.2 restart run 2: the persisted per-node scale replayed at 125%
